Hey, Toru! Your timing couldn't be better! It's about Miyamura. I was wondering if you-

74
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,400
Are you serious?

75
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:18,940
My heart's still in the process of healing. Give me time!

76
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:23,020
Wait! Some help you are!

77
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:28,420
You know, trying to find out a person's first name would be so exhausting.

78
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:33,700
Kyoko, what's wrong, huh? I hope the curry's not putting that sour look on your face.

79
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,120
We've had microwave curry three days in a row.

80
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:40,800
Oh, hey! There's no school tomorrow, if memory serves. Is your friend coming?

81
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:42,820
Um, probably.

82
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:45,060
You think so?

83
00:05:45,400 --> 00:05:48,300
Oh, that's great! I'm really excited now!

84
00:05:48,300 --> 00:05:51,420
It's not like he's coming over here to hang out with you, you know.

85
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:55,580
Wait! There's a good chance he'll tell Mom his name!

86
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:56,380
Got him!

87
00:05:56,380 --> 00:06:03,540
You're finally here!

88
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:06,900
So nice to meet you! Don't be shy, please! Come in!

89
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:08,760
Um, thank you.

90
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:13,880
Wow. This must be Hori's mom. What a surprise.

91
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,900
Uh, I brought some sweets.

92
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,440
You did? So thoughtful.

93
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:22,020
Sorry, but Kyoko isn't here.

94
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,720
She's out and about running some errands right now.

95
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:27,260
Oh, she's told me so much about you, though.

96
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:28,640
Hi, Mom!

97
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,040
He's home late today.

98
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:32,960
Hey! How have you been, bro?

99
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:36,520
I see! That name really suits you.

100
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:39,420
I would love to stay and chat, honest.

101
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:42,060
But I sadly have to get back to work.

102
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:44,640
That's okay. I'll be heading out soon, too.

103
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:47,880
You're leaving already? But you just got here!

104
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:49,480
Yeah.

105
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:52,140
I appreciate you helping out when you can.

106
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:55,260
Well, sure.

107
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:58,460
Huh? Where'd Mom go?

108
00:06:58,580 --> 00:06:59,280
Where else?

109
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:01,260
She's at work.

110
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,800
So, which one you want to eat?

111
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:05,120
Strawberry, please!

112
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:06,200
That witch of a woman!

113
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:10,120
She wanted her stupid one-on-one time with him, so she sent me on errands!

114
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:13,500
Man, the last time someone called me my first name, I was in the sixth grade.

115
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:14,880
It felt kind of weird.

116
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:17,460
Wait, what?

117
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,320
Talking about your mom. She used my first name.

118
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,500
That's not what I meant!

119
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,460
Do you mean how she used it?

120
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,180
Uh-huh, uh-huh, uh-huh, uh-huh.

121
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:28,600
Just as a greeting. She didn't use it that much, but still.

122
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:33,340
Have the two of us ever had a conversation where we were both on the same page?

123
00:07:34,120 --> 00:07:35,280
Come on!

124
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:37,240
Come on! That's not what I meant, either.

125
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:41,040
You know, recently, you've been acting really strange.

126
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,780
Me? What? No way!

127
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:46,200
Well, watching guys change clothes is pretty weird.

128
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:48,000
But I had a reason for that.

129
00:07:49,120 --> 00:07:49,860
Hold on.

130
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:53,000
Hori, do you have a crush?

131
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Hori, do you have a crush?

132
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Mm-hmm.

133
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:58,100
No.

134
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:07,880
Wait, my name? That's what you've been so worried about?

135
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:11,780
All because of a stupid name? You are something else.

136
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,660
That's one of the lamest things I've ever heard.

137
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:15,800
Excuse me for not knowing how to ask you.

138
00:08:15,820 --> 00:08:18,640
I'm stealing your pen real quick. Give me a sec.

139
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:20,220
Ed Lamo, what's your name?

140
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:23,080
That's the crush! That's the...

141
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:29,440
Izumi Miyamura.

142
00:08:30,480 --> 00:08:31,380
Ah, forgot.

143
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,520
Pronunciation. Give it back.

144
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:34,400
I can pronounce it!

145
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:34,980
Wait.

146
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:37,840
I'll go ahead and hang on to this note.

147
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,080
Just in case I forget it again.

148
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:43,280
Oh, that sucks. Is my name really that forgettable?

149
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:45,040
No! I said just in case!

150
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,740
You'll remember it easier if you say it.

151
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:48,780
Mm-

152
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,000
I-

153
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,060
Izumi.

154
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:52,220
Right.

155
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:54,320
There you go.

156
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,000
Uh-

157
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:00,980
That felt super awkward.

158
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:02,940
I'll just keep calling you Miyamura!

159
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:05,300
Jeez, what was that for, Hori?

160
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:05,780
Uh-

161
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,600
Wait, hold the phone!

162
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:10,300
You're as clueless about my first name as I was about yours!

163
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:10,780
No.

164
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,080
It's Kyoko.

165
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:17,460
The hole I'm digging keeps getting deeper!

166
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:19,620
Hori says the dumbest things sometimes.

167
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,060
Ugh!

168
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,300
What are you waiting for? Go ahead and laugh!

169
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:24,040
I'm good.

170
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:25,640
You'll just get mad if I laugh.

171
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:26,720
You're damn right I will!

172
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:29,500
Uh, you don't play fair!

173
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,160
Uh-

174
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:31,160
Uh-

175
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:43,380
I'm sorry. Really. I can only imagine how busy you are.

176
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:46,880
It's totally cool. I'd do anything for you, Sengoku.

177
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:53,360
Thanks. You're a true lifesaver. Sakura, I trust you'll handle these?

178
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:54,340
Of course.

179
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:58,840
It's amazing how much smoother things go when you've got capable people on the job.

180
00:09:59,300 --> 00:10:00,800
Yeah, I guess so.

181
00:10:00,860 --> 00:10:05,740
Which is why, if you don't mind, I, uh, I have another favor I'd like to ask of you.

182
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:06,160
What?

183
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:12,380
Please? I know it's inconvenient, but we're only asking because the student council has so much to do.

184
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:16,620
You're good. I know how it can be, so yeah, no worries.

185
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,840
Your eyes!

186
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:22,720
Girl!

187
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:24,260
Are they bad?

188
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:28,880
This what the student council dumped off on you?

189
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:29,740
Yeah.

190
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:33,640
Why are you stuck doing their work? You're not one of them.

191
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:37,520
They have a lot of new members, so they're having a hard time getting things done.

192
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:39,220
Simple as that, huh?

193
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:42,680
It just feels kind of messed up that they have you do such important stuff.

194
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,840
It's like they're using you and you don't even care.

195
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:48,260
Because I don't care. It's just, they need the extra help.

196
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:50,180
That's the thing. You should care.

197
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:51,880
Ori's got it pretty rough.

198
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:52,540
Hmm.

199
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:58,180
As for us, we stand on the sidelines and watch because we're too stupid to do anything else.

200
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:01,380
The truth hurts. At least we recognize it, though.

201
00:11:01,620 --> 00:11:03,400
And the press is at the top of the class.

202
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:04,100
He is?

203
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:06,800
He's got a fairly big fan club, too.

204
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:10,940
It's highly possible Ori's only helping him out because she secretly likes him.

205
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,180
Yoo-hoo! Ori!

206
00:11:21,180 --> 00:11:24,320
Oh! Hey, Ayusaki!

207
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:25,960
Huh?

208
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:33,980
Here are the files and notebooks I worked on. Be careful, since they're heavy.

209
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:35,440
Remy will be!

210
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:36,780
Thanks, Ori!

211
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,780
That pink-haired princess's job did gorgeous.

212
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:42,660
And she's also President Sengoku's girlfriend.

213
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:44,380
It's no fair when two hotties date!

214
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,620
Ayusaki's another member of the council.

215
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,920
I don't think she does much work, though.

216
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,820
She's more like a mascot than anything.

217
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:52,240
Wait.

218
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:55,640
So what you're saying is they're pushing all this hot chick's work on Hori?

219
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:56,620
Toru, please!

220
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:57,760
Don't put it like that.

221
00:11:58,140 --> 00:11:59,720
Because it's not too far from the truth.

222
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:02,320
The work I just did was Ayusaki's.

223
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:05,860
They're 100% using her and she's okay with it?

224
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:16,080
Well, I think I'm gonna head home.

225
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,280
Bye.

226
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,720
Is she actually alright?

227
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:22,500
I hope so.

228
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:28,160
Cake makes people feel better.

229
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:29,660
Maybe I'll bake her one.

230
00:12:32,220 --> 00:12:32,980
I'm sorry.

231
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:34,300
You didn't get hurt, did you?

232
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:39,460
Hey, watch where you're going, jerk face!

233
00:12:39,620 --> 00:12:39,940
Huh?

234
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:41,840
But you're the one who ran into me!

235
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:42,560
Remy doesn't have time for this nonsense!

236
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,420
Why are you sitting there when you could help?

237
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:47,600
Sakura's gonna yell at me again for being late,

238
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:49,160
and it's not even Remy's fault!

239
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:52,600
Wait up!

240
00:12:52,680 --> 00:12:52,920
Hey!

241
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:55,020
Whatever it is, it can't be that important.

242
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:56,100
So throw it out for me, okay?

243
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:56,960
Buh-bye!

244
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:03,260
Guess I know what talking with the pink wall feels like now.

245
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:32,100
What gives?

246
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:33,240
I told you!

247
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:36,060
I gave you every single page that I worked on!

248
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,640
So you say.

249
00:13:37,980 --> 00:13:41,520
But there are pages missing, and we haven't been able to find them anywhere.

250
00:13:41,900 --> 00:13:42,760
What's this about?

251
00:13:43,600 --> 00:13:43,940
Ah!

252
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:44,720
Miyamura!

253
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:45,960
Thank goodness you're here!

254
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:46,840
Please help!

255
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:47,520
It's Hori!

256
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:48,860
What's Hori?

257
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:51,120
The student council's given her flack for some reason!

258
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:54,940
I returned everything you gave me yesterday!

259
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:57,000
The budget paperwork should have been in there too!

260
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:58,280
Ask Aisaki!

261
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,260
She saw it!

262
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:02,960
Remy already said that she didn't see it there.

263
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:06,700
Did you double check, or is there a chance you could be mistaken?

264
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:09,160
Well, either way, you guys are-

265
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:11,240
Still at fault, and of course you have a point.

266
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:17,540
That is, if the missing budget report was actually in that pile, you have no one to blame but yourself otherwise.

267
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:20,700
So tell me, do you know for certain it was there?

268
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:24,720
Yes, I do.

269
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:30,180
But to be honest, I was so tired, I can't remember.

270
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:32,320
Wow, Hori screwed up.

271
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:36,580
So how far behind are they now that she lost those reports?

272
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:40,220
I don't know, but I feel super sorry for the president.

273
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,340
So if this is in fact your fault, all I want is an apology from you.

274
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:45,360
Is that so hard?

275
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:48,140
Shut it, asshole!

276
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:50,380
You're only making things worse.

277
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:51,720
Leave her alone!

278
00:14:52,040 --> 00:14:53,460
Hori finished that budget report!

279
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:55,460
I know because I saw her do it!

280
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:57,360
I also saw her turning it in!

281
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,980
All she has to do is apologize to him.

282
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:02,940
What's the big deal?

283
00:15:03,160 --> 00:15:05,400
Three syllables should not be this hard to say.

284
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:07,220
Ishikawa.

285
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,620
Gonna hold me back too?

286
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,140
Actually, I was hoping you could do the holding.

287
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:12,520
This shouldn't take too long.

288
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:13,880
Go ahead.

289
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,680
It's your move.

290
00:15:20,700 --> 00:15:21,140
I...

291
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:22,620
Don't have to apologize.

292
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:25,360
Hori, you don't owe them a thing.

293
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:26,660
Huh?

294
00:15:31,460 --> 00:15:32,800
And what do you want?

295
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:33,460
Mr. President...

296
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:44,160
What the hell do you think you're doing?

297
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:46,120
My poor Sengoku!

298
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:49,560
Just so you know, violence is unacceptable.

299
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:51,500
What possessed you to do such a...

300
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:54,200
Is this the report that went missing?

301
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,380
Yeah, that's the one.

302
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:57,860
But why do you have it?

303
00:15:58,300 --> 00:16:00,080
It was left behind in the hall yesterday.

304
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:03,860
Ayasaki said I should trash it because it wasn't important.

305
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:05,380
Remy said no such thing!

306
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:05,680
Oh!

307
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:14,940
Oh!

308
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:17,280
Guess that did happen.

309
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:21,060
Remy!

310
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:29,780
You guys!

311
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:30,980
I'm so sorry!

312
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:35,000
So they accused Hori even though she didn't do it?

313
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:36,700
What even happened?

314
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:37,900
Who knows?

315
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:52,900
All's well that ends well.

316
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:54,020
As they say.

317
00:16:54,940 --> 00:16:57,160
Five more seconds and I would have been in tears.

318
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:00,860
Anybody who has their crap together like you would never do that!

319
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:02,340
Oh, thank you.

320
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,880
Though I guess the one I should really be grateful for is Miyamura.

321
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:06,960
So thanks!

322
00:17:09,020 --> 00:17:10,260
I'm glad it worked out.

323
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:11,420
One question.

324
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:15,740
If you had the missing report the entire time, why'd you need to headbutt the president?

325
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:17,200
I didn't need to.

326
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,620
He was just really pissing me off.

327
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:26,660
While we're on the topic, I've been wondering, does the president have any dirt on you, Hori?

328
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:32,080
I mean, if a guy asks you to do something, you do it without a second thought.

329
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:32,580
But why?

330
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:33,640
Yeah, why?

331
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:35,160
Hori?

332
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:37,100
Don't Hori me.

333
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:40,720
It's because the student council's so busy and I really want to help.

334
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:41,920
Sengoku's my friend.

335
00:17:42,180 --> 00:17:44,560
So it's just one childhood pal helping another.

336
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:46,620
Boo-hoo!

337
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,880
You're the biggest crybaby I know!

338
00:17:48,980 --> 00:17:49,340
Oh!

339
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:50,660
You're hurting me, Giyoko!

340
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:53,740
These are the grossest things in the world!

341
00:17:54,560 --> 00:17:56,300
Rock, paper, scissors!

342
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:59,700
The moment we get to high school, I promise you my dog days will be done.

343
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:01,400
Is that a fact?

344
00:18:01,940 --> 00:18:03,780
You think of yourself as my dog?

345
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:05,820
Wow, who knew?

346
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:09,280
Laugh now, but you'll grow to respect me.

347
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:12,120
I'll have a normal happy time in high school, you'll see!

348
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,180
Oh, I will?

349
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:17,060
If you try to tear me down, I'll tell everyone how much you bullied me in the past.

350
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:17,760
Ha!

351
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:18,900
Bullied?

352
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:21,360
Yes, bullied! You're doing it right now!

353
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:26,740
That's taunting, not bullying, but that said, you do have a point there.

354
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:31,980
Hmph. All right then. Come high school, we're equals.

355
00:18:32,440 --> 00:18:33,760
Ha! Ha! Ha! Ha! Ha!

356
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:35,760
Ugh.

357
00:18:36,620 --> 00:18:39,720
Seriously, guys, I've known that kid for forever.

358
00:18:40,180 --> 00:18:42,200
He definitely has dirt on her.

359
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:49,040
Oh, hey!

360
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:51,540
Good morning, Prez.

361
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:52,740
Ah!

362
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:54,920
Good morning to you too, sir!

363
00:18:56,980 --> 00:19:01,260
I may have recovered from that day, but Sengoku was traumatized.

364
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:14,800
Miyamura, did you know Hori's birthday is just around the corner?

365
00:19:15,140 --> 00:19:16,720
Well, I do now.

366
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:18,480
March 25th, to be exact.

367
00:19:19,180 --> 00:19:20,980
Ah, so it's during spring break.

368
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:23,600
I'm on the fence about getting her something.

369
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:28,380
You know, how annoying would it be to get a gift from the guy she rejected?

370
00:19:28,820 --> 00:19:30,120
I don't think she'd find it annoying.

371
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:32,700
Because, I mean, why would she?

372
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:33,540
It's her birthday.

373
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:37,480
But then problem number two is that I have no earthly idea what to get her.

374
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:39,700
Thought that counts.

375
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:41,380
So, get her whatever.

376
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:42,740
Maybe jewelry?

377
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:43,640
Jewelry?

378
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:45,420
From the dude she turned down?

379
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,140
What about something for her desk?

380
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:49,660
I thought if anyone knew what kind of stuff she likes, it would be you!

381
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:56,680
Um, if I was gonna give Hori a present, what would I give her?

382
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:14,060
Hey, since it's spring break, do you think my bro will come and visit every single day?

383
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:16,800
I don't think he'll come here every day.

384
00:20:17,660 --> 00:20:21,260
Just keep in mind that eventually he's going to stop visiting us all together.

385
00:20:21,840 --> 00:20:24,500
Aw, well when is that gonna be, sissy?

386
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:26,600
When you graduate high school?

387
00:20:29,740 --> 00:20:32,180
When will Miyamura stop coming to my house?

388
00:20:33,560 --> 00:20:34,460
I don't know.

389
00:20:35,220 --> 00:20:36,900
I wish I could tell you, but I can't.

390
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:41,820
Just wondering, but do you think you'll be sad when he stops visiting?

391
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:44,340
I'm gonna be super sad.

392
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:46,720
Hey, Hori.

393
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:49,820
Yeah, me too.

394
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:52,040
I'll be pretty bummed out.

395
00:20:53,740 --> 00:20:56,220
You could be a little more honest if you ask me.

396
00:20:56,740 --> 00:20:57,980
What do you know?

397
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:06,360
Happy birthday!

398
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,160
And may you have many more.

399
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:10,240
Oh yeah, it is my birthday.

400
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:13,640
I totally forgot about it because we were on spring break.

401
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:14,920
Oh my gosh.

402
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,680
Here, this one's from me.

403
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:17,940
Happy birthday!

404
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:23,900
A CD of the best pop songs!

405
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:26,220
This is what people our age are listening to, right?

406
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:27,100
Awesome!

407
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:30,180
Well, they're the ones I like at least.

408
00:21:30,180 --> 00:21:32,780
It's very sweet.

409
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:34,460
Thanks so much.

410
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:37,520
How strange.

411
00:21:38,560 --> 00:21:42,820
I didn't say a word, but he somehow knew this was what I wanted.

412
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:45,000
Such a weirdo.

413
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:56,060
Since today is my birthday, that means spring break's almost over.

414
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:56,620
Awesome.

415
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:01,460
Yeah.

416
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:02,360
Yeah.

417
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:13,060
Guess we'll be 30 or soon.

418
00:22:13,060 --> 00:22:43,040
Thank you.

419
00:22:43,060 --> 00:23:13,040
Thank you.

420
00:23:13,060 --> 00:23:15,060
Thank you.

421
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:45,060
Thank you.

